  <note id="GUID-74F52CDA-A3CE-461A-8506-8760BD27017D"> All values are subject to change: 
	 <p><sup>1</sup> C: compute tile, GCD: graphics tile, HUB: hub tile, PCD: Peripheral Control Die tile, P: passive tile 
	 </p> 
	 <p> 
		<sup>2</sup> Z-Height value is the Max Z-Height Pre-SMT, refer NVL Package Mechanical Drawings (#<xref format="https" scope="external" href="https://cdrdv2.intel.com/v1/dl/getContent/858127">858127</xref>) 
	 </p> 
	 <p><sup>3</sup> Max Operating Temperature is the maximum operating temperature allowed as reported by temperature sensors. Instantaneous temperature may exceed this value for short durations. Note that maximum observable temperature is configurable by system vendors and can be design specific. 
	 </p> 
	 <p><sup>4</sup> For Maximum Turbo Frequency vs Temperature, refer to the 
		<xref scope="local" format="dita" href="GUID-2C35BBFE-4B21-4271-AAD4-CEFE9145B25F.dita">Section 2.1</xref> for definition. 
	 </p> 
	 <p><sup>5</sup>≥25W recommended for 16C designs to take advantage of performance scaling. Customers with designs inflight targeting a PL1 between 15-25W for H16C will continue to be supported in NVL. 
	 </p> 
  </note> 
